---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How the GitHub Apps Directory Works"
  description="A plain-language explanation of how Must-Have GitHub Apps checks permissions, pricing, privacy, setup, and sources."
>
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1 class="display">A simple guide to GitHub tools.</h1><p>
      This independent directory helps people choose tools for their GitHub projects.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container detail-content">
    <h2>What this site does</h2><p>
      It explains what a tool does, what it can access, what it costs, how much work it adds, and
      what its limits are. Each entry includes official sources and dates.
    </p>
    <h2>How we check entries</h2><p>
      Automated checks find broken links, formatting problems, and build errors. A person checks the
      facts before an entry is changed. AI tools may suggest improvements, but they do not replace
      that review.
    </p>
    <h2>Why a second review matters</h2><p>
      The source project protects its main branch. The person who makes a change cannot approve that
      same change. A second maintainer or trusted reviewer must approve it. This protects the
      project from accidental or unsafe self-approval.
    </p>
    <h2>What we do not promise</h2><p>
      A listing is not a security audit or a promise that a tool will suit every project. A passing
      scan is useful evidence, not proof that a project is safe. If a fact cannot be checked, we say
      so.
    </p>
    <h2>Help improve the directory</h2><p>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/jordan-thirkle/must-have-github-apps/issues/new?template=app-recommendation.yml"
        >Suggest a tool</a
      > or <a
        href="https://github.com/jordan-thirkle/must-have-github-apps/issues/new?template=directory-maintenance.yml"
        >report an outdated fact</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/jordan-thirkle/must-have-github-apps"
        >★ Star this project on GitHub</a
      >
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
